  "answer": "I'll treat this as a new storefront cart limit and start from the Feature playbook so the quantity rule is designed before any code changes.The cart limit sits on two subsystems, so I\u2019m tracing storefront cart writes and merchant configuration in parallel before choosing a design.Storefront cart writes go through `ShoppingCartApi` (`POST /cart`, `PUT /cart/{code}`, `POST /cart/{code}/multi`). Merchant settings are loaded per request from `MerchantConfigurationService`, so a new key can change without a restart. I\u2019m waiting on the rest of the cart and configuration traces before locking the check into one place.The limit belongs in the cart facade, checked against the quantity the request would store, and read from merchant configuration on each call. I\u2019ll add that guard before any line is written.Storefront cart writes now refuse a line above the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting, or 99 when that setting is absent. `CartLineQuantityLimits` reads the setting on each request, so a change applies without a restart. `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi` return HTTP 400 through `RestApiException` before the cart is changed, including when an add sums onto an existing line. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Model the Domain kept that cap in one type instead of a separate check in each endpoint.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\":[\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=CartLineQuantityLimitsTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"],\"result\":\"passed\",\"could_not_verify\":[\"HTTP 400 on the live cart endpoints and that the stored cart is unchanged, because ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest was not run\"],\"missing\":[\"an integration fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and asserts the cart row is unchanged after a 400\"]}The cart and merchant-configuration traces match the change already in place. Storefront writes go through `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl`, and `getMerchantConfiguration` hits the database on each call with no cache. The quantity cap runs before any line is deleted or saved, so no further code change is needed.",
